            <ArticleTitle>[A rare cause of obstruction: hernia through the hiatus of Winslow. Apropos of 3 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>598-602</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Exceptional pathology whose preoperative diagnosis is based upon clinical and radiological signs; the herniation through the foramen of Winslow is a variety of internal herniation. About three recent cases observed in the service, it seemed interesting to see, reviewing literature, what are the diagnostic characters and therapeutic modalities knowing difficulties because of a quasi exclusive vascular collect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
